WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.330
Still mad about how Game of Thrones went down?

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.910
Fear not — House of the Dragon has got your
back.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.523
Keep watching to find out why you should give
it a shot.

00:00:08.523 --> 00:00:12.680
Game of Thrones took a heavy hit following
the release of its eighth season.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:17.460
The show's final episodes were panned by fans,
many of whom criticized the story's rushed

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.289
pacing and many attempts to subvert audiences'
expectations.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:22.640
So what went wrong?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.630
Well, for one thing, the White Walkers were
defeated in one episode — after eight seasons

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.820
of build-up.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.090
And if you thought the Night King's stare
down with Jon Snow in Season 5's "Hardhome"

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.020
guaranteed an epic final fight between the
two, well, think again.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.290
Arya Stark is the one to take out the Night
King in the show, while Jon is preoccupied

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.570
with the undead dragon Viserion.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.870
But that's not all.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.800
The revelation that Jon is actually Aegon
Targaryen, trueborn son of Rhaegar Targaryen

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.120
and Lyanna Stark, ultimately leads to nothing.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.990
Jon never ascends the Iron Throne or fulfills
the prophecy of the Prince That Was Promised.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:03.310
Meanwhile, Daenerys Targaryen flips from Mhysa
to Mad Queen in one harrowing episode, which

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.920
sees her slaughter the civilians of King's
Landing with dragonfire.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.579
Oh, and Jaime Lannister abandons Brienne of
Tarth to die with his sister and lover, Cersei.

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:18.329
In the end, Bran Stark emerges from the ashes
as the new King of Westeros, because… reasons.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:21.009
"And who has a better story…

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.229
than Bran the Broken?"

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:28.740
Naturally, all of this led many Game of Thrones
fans to vow that they were finished with the

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.091
once-esteemed fantasy franchise.

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:36.719
So far, only one aspect of the Game of Thrones
finale has been confirmed to come from Martin

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:38.420
himself: King Bran.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:42.859
During a 2019 interview published by HBO,
actor Isaac Hempstead Wright stated:

00:01:42.859 --> 00:01:47.639
"David [Benioff] and Dan [Weiss] told me there
were two things George R.R.

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:53.304
Martin had planned for Bran, and that was
the Hodor revelation, and that he would be king.

00:01:53.304 --> 00:01:58.469
So that's pretty special to be directly involved
in something that is part of George's vision."

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:02.899
Unless Martin changes his mind, fans can expect
to see Bran on the throne in the books as

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:04.069
well as in the show.

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:05.679
Everything else, however?

00:02:05.679 --> 00:02:07.259
That remains questionable.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:11.370
Martin has even said that fans know "an ending,"
but not "the ending."

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:16.750
It's certainly easy for fans to remain hopeful
for a more satisfying conclusion to the novels.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:22.110
Fortunately, House of the Dragon seems to
be rebuilding bridges with its spurned audience.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:27.400
A prequel to Game of Thrones, House of the
Dragon takes place 172 years before Daenerys

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.760
Targaryen's birth and documents one of the
most turbulent times in her family's history:

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.030
the period of civil war known as the Dance
of the Dragons.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:40.939
For fans who loved the political drama and
scandals of Game Of Thrones, this is the perfect

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:43.700
successor show to scratch that itch.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.579
During its premiere episode, House of the
Dragon places as much emphasis on the Song

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:50.360
of Ice and Fire as it does Game of Thrones.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:54.370
In "The Heirs of the Dragon," King Viserys
informs his daughter Rhaenyra about a prophetic

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:59.569
dream of their ancestor Aegon's that spurred
him to conquer Westeros with his dragon, Balerion

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:00.700
the Black Dread.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.450
"Aegon called his dream the Song of Ice and
Fire."

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:08.319
King Viserys passes on Aegon's vision of a
"terrible winter, gusting out of the distant

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:12.870
North," which prompted the conqueror to create
the Iron Throne and unify the kingdoms under

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.300
Targaryen rule.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.530
It's an interesting tidbit that further fleshes
out the story of the Others.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:23.659
But why did the showrunners, Ryan Condal and
Miguel Sapochnik, choose to include a prophecy

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:29.165
about the White Walkers in a show about House
Targaryen — particularly in its first episode?

00:03:29.165 --> 00:03:34.724
As it turns out, Aegon the Conqueror's prophecy
comes from none other than George R.R. Martin.

00:03:34.724 --> 00:03:38.900
The author confirmed his involvement with
House of the Dragon early on, while showrunner

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.030
Ryan Condal spoke to Esquire about collaborating
with Martin.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.030
He said:

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.379
"George hired me, and I came to this as a
fan.

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:48.439
He was very involved with the beginning of
the show.

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:50.930
Obviously, it does not exist without him.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.850
He wrote the original source material."

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:53.950
Condal continued:

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:59.090
"This was the successor show that I think
he was most interested in, of all the ones

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.310
that HBO was considering and exploring.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:06.420
Certainly, [in] the very beginning in [the]
conceptual phase, George was very involved."

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.370
In an interview with The New York Times, Martin
compared his involvement with House of the

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:14.329
Dragon to Game of Thrones, remarking how he
was kept "out of the loop" during the later

00:04:14.329 --> 00:04:15.610
seasons of Thrones.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.610
He claimed:

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:21.009
"By Season 5 and 6, and certainly 7 and 8,
I was pretty much out of the loop.

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:24.080
I don't know [why] – you have to ask [showrunners]
Dan and Dave."

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.930
With Martin at the helm, House of the Dragon
offers the chance to tell a story more faithful

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.720
to the author's original vision.

00:04:30.997 --> 00:04:32.720
Thanks to George R.R.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.400
Martin's involvement, House of the Dragon
seems to be bridging the gap between show

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.000
and book canon.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.650
For example, Aegon's prophecy makes no mention
of anything to symbolize Arya Stark as the

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.650
savior of humanity.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.580
"Stick 'em with the pointy end."

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:51.020
The last scions of House Targaryen don't realy
phase the Night King in Game of Thrones, as

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:56.660
Daenerys and Drogon quickly discover the icy
villain is fireproof, while Jon is overwhelmed

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:01.250
by undead soldiers before he can take a swing
at any White Walkers.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:05.539
It's certainly possible that Aegon's prophecy
in House of the Dragon isn't supposed to foreshadow

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:07.070
the Game of Thrones finale.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:11.880
In 2019, before Season 8 aired, Martin revealed
to Entertainment Weekly that he hadn't read

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.889
any scripts for the final season, stating:

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:18.260
"There's a lot of minor-character [arcs] they'll
be coming up with on their own.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.020
And, of course, they passed me several years
ago.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.400
There may be important discrepancies."

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.919
More recently, Martin confirmed on his blog
that his ending will be different, adding:

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:32.610
"Not all of the characters who survived until
the end of Game of Thrones will survive until

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:36.670
the end of A Song of Ice and Fire, and not
all of the characters who died on Game of

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.630
Thrones will die in A Song of Ice And Fire."

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:44.639
Before House of the Dragon, HBO almost greenlit
another prequel to follow Season 8 of Game

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:45.639
of Thrones.

00:05:45.639 --> 00:05:50.569
The planned series, titled Bloodmoon, was
to take place 8,000 years before the events

00:05:50.569 --> 00:05:54.690
of the original show, during an era known
as the Age of Heroes.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.069
What was Bloodmoon about?

00:05:56.069 --> 00:06:00.950
In summary: the White Walkers.This prequel
would have depicted the first Long Night eight

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:05.039
centuries before the Night King's defeat at
Winterfell, with the White Walkers descending

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:08.260
on humanity from the far North for the very
first time.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.669
According to HBO, Bloodmoon was going to be
seriously epic in scope.

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:14.060
The first press release stated:

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:19.099
"From the horrifying secrets of Westeros's
history to the true origin of the white walkers,

00:06:19.099 --> 00:06:21.819
the mysteries of the East to the Starks of
legend...

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:24.259
it's not the story we think we know."

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:27.610
Jane Goldman was to serve as showrunner alongside
George R.R.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:31.960
Martin as an executive producer, while Naomi
Watts had been cast in a lead role.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.449
Sadly, Bloodmoon never made it past production.

00:06:34.449 --> 00:06:39.050
A pilot episode was filmed, but the series
was shelved in favor of House of the Dragon.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:42.889
Given that Bloodmoon was supposed to focus
on the Long Night and the origin of the White

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:47.020
Walkers, it's possible that Aegon's prophecy
— or whatever inspired it — would have

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.505
been heavily involved in that series.

00:06:49.505 --> 00:06:55.509
It's worth noting that HBO doesn't necessarily
need Bloodmoon to redeem the series finale.

00:06:55.509 --> 00:06:58.099
Along with a slate of prequel shows, George
R.R.

00:06:58.099 --> 00:07:01.730
Martin confirmed on his blog that a sequel
to Game of Thrones is currently in the pipe works.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.909
Not much is known so far about the sequel,
but what fans do know is that the planned

00:07:05.909 --> 00:07:10.609
series is Jon Snow-centric, with actor Kit
Harington leading the project.

00:07:10.609 --> 00:07:12.974
"You know nothing, Jon Snow."

00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:17.560
Official news of the Jon Snow sequel first
broke in a piece for The Hollywood Reporter.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:22.130
Emilia Clarke later verified in an interview
with the BBC that Harrington essentially created

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.979
the show, and that he is "in it from the ground
up."

00:07:24.979 --> 00:07:28.349
There are no guarantees that the Jon Snow
sequel will make it out of pre-production.

00:07:28.349 --> 00:07:33.879
Still, if the series does make it to the small
screen, it could retcon parts of Season 8;

00:07:33.879 --> 00:07:37.729
it might even correspond with Aegon's prophecy
in House of the Dragon.

00:07:37.729 --> 00:07:44.190
A sequel starring Jon Snow, aka Aegon Targaryan,
could very well feature the return of the

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.441
White Walkers, led by a new icy villain for
him to face.

00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:52.319
Game of Thrones could also be brought back
to the small screen in animation.

00:07:52.319 --> 00:07:53.330
According to George R.R.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:58.080
Martin's blog, an animated prequel set in
the distant land of Essos is also in the early

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.669
stages of pre-production.

00:07:59.669 --> 00:08:05.754
The Golden Empire of Yi Ti, inspired by Imperial
China, predates both Old Valyria and the Long Night.

00:08:05.754 --> 00:08:09.919
Some fans speculate that it was the Gemstone
Emperors of Yi Ti who taught the Valyrians

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:11.460
how to control dragons.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:16.389
Corlys Velaryon made the long, perilous voyage
to Yi Ti in his youth, something that viewers

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:19.069
could witness if his prequel series is greenlit.

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:24.260
If HBO branches into animation with its Yi
Ti series, then it's also possible fans could

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:28.490
see an animated adaptation of A Song of Ice
And Fire in the future.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.740
Animation requires a less hefty budget, too
— something that might appeal to HBO after

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:37.039
it spent $90 million on the final season of
Game of Thrones.

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:41.930
This is one way that Thrones could return
bigger and bloodier than ever.

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:47.140
The inclusion of Aegon's prophecy to House
of the Dragon doesn't appear to be a fluke.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:51.120
A Weeks Ahead Trailer released on the official
Game of Thrones YouTube channel has teased

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.950
even more prophecies in the show.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:58.180
In the teaser, Milly Alcock's Rhaenyra Targaryen
appears to be reading more of Aegon the Conqueror's

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.159
documented prophetic dreams as she states:

00:09:02.159 --> 00:09:07.342
"From my blood come the Prince That Was Promised."

00:09:07.342 --> 00:09:11.100
This is big news for readers of the books.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:15.560
In the second novel, A Clash of Kings, Daenerys
ventures into the House of the Undying to

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.100
seek counsel from the mysterious warlocks
of Qarth.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:23.060
Daenerys consumes a psychedelic substance
known as Shade of the Evening and experiences

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.070
multiple prophetic visions.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:30.510
In one, a brutalized woman represents war-torn
Westeros; another features the Wolf King at

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.370
a feast, foreshadowing the Red Wedding.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:37.450
Several others include snippets from the past
and the future of Martin's world.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:41.470
One such moment includes her brother Rhaegar
talking with an unknown woman about their

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.920
newborn son.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:46.250
During this scene, Rhaegar speaks the same
words that Rhaenyra speaks in the House of

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:47.430
the Dragon trailer.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:51.060
It seems that House of the Dragon will be
tackling this crucial plot thread sometime

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:56.185
in the future, despite the fact that it apparently
has little to do with the main events of the show.

00:09:56.185 --> 00:10:01.110
With the runaway success of House of the Dragon,
the future of the Game of Thrones franchise

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.292
suddenly looks more optimistic.

00:10:03.292 --> 00:10:09.440
George R.R. Martin's enthusiasm for the prequel is gradually
encouraging fans' trust again after the disastrous

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:14.370
final season of Game of Thrones — and the
extra efforts taken to adhere to book canon

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.260
aren't exactly hurting, either.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:21.000
HBO seems to be focusing on filling out the
world, too, with various prequels and spin-offs

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.130
set in Westeros and Essos lined up.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:27.510
If any of them match the early success of
House of the Dragon, then it's likely the

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:32.750
streaming titan will go all in on building
a potential Martin Cinematic Universe.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:37.640
If that happens, then revisiting the apocalyptic
threat from the far North sounds far too good

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.139
a spectacle to pass on.

00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:43.730
Whether it's down to a Jon Snow sequel, another
prequel, or simply a plot thread followed

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:48.230
by House of the Dragon, there's a good chance
that the events of the final season of Game

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:52.250
of Thrones will one day feel like nothing
more than a bad dream.

